{{> Top frame}}
<header>
  <p class="kicker">Go deeper</p>
  <h1>Live</h1>
  <p class="lede">Hypermedia: the server sends HTML, and a few attributes make the page
  live. No JavaScript of yours; <a href="https://data-star.dev">Datastar</a> does the
  wiring.</p>
</header>

<section class="like">
  <button data-on:click="@post('/like')">♥</button>
  <p>{{> LikeCount likes}} likes, every click in this clone</p>
</section>

<section class="turn-box">
  <h2>Your turn</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><p>Click the heart. The browser posts to <code>/like</code>; <code>like!</code> in
    <code>main.roc</code> counts it in the database and answers with a server-sent event
    holding <code>templates/LikeCount.rocstache</code>, rendered. Datastar puts it where the element with
    the same <code>id</code> is.</p></li>
    <li><p>Reload the page. The count is still there: each click went through
    <code>Sqlite.write!</code> and <code>Sqlite.commit!</code> into <code>tutor.db</code>, and the
    page reads it back as it is made.</p></li>
    <li><p>Edit <code>templates/LikeCount.rocstache</code>: make the number <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code>, keep
    the <code>id</code>. A fragment is a template like any other: on screen as you save.</p></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>The whole loop</h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;button data-on:click="@post('/like')"&gt;♥&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  <pre><code>stream = Sse.start!(request, [])?
Sse.send!(stream, Rocstache.patch!(LikeCount.template({ count: count })))?
Sse.end!(stream)</code></pre>
  <p>The same template value a page response carries, sent as a patch. A stream can stay
  open and send many: the Speed page's race sends a thousand.</p>
</section>
{{> Bottom nav}}
